(7367023, 1151236, 30364, '<td valign="top">Hard to credit the cool reception given this photograph.  That anyone who loves photography could fail to love this. You must despair, sometimes?  Me, I''d like to confiscate 68 cameras, and revoke their owners'' carry permits for life.</td>', 'Hard to credit the cool reception given this photograph.  That anyone who loves photography could fail to love this. You must despair, sometimes?  Me, I''d like to confiscate 68 cameras, and revoke their owners'' carry permits for life.', '2015-06-19 10:58:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7367189, 1151236, 100393, '<td valign="top">Many thanks for the kind comments on this image - I''m glad it struck a chord with some of you folks. It means a lot.</td>', 'Many thanks for the kind comments on this image - I''m glad it struck a chord with some of you folks. It means a lot.', '2015-06-19 14:29:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7373821, 1151827, 115814, '<td valign="top">Hi Zita - this is coming as a Critique Club member - getting to some backlogged requests. <br/> <br/>I was surprised that this didn''t do better, I gave it a six and considered bumping it near the end. It has a unusual POV and the color palette (especially in the top third of the image is terrific - the yellows are perfect against the green and blue. I suspect what didn''t work so well for voters was the heavily weighted dark bottom portion that is an artifact of the POV. There''s also the contrast of larger dominant shapes at the top and more detailed busy shapes at the bottom. This tends to create ambiguity about where the viewer''s central focus of attention should be. I liked the effect of imbalance in the two halves, it may have been distracting to others.</td>', 'Hi Zita - this is coming as a Critique Club member - getting to some backlogged requests.  I was surprised that this didn''t do better, I gave it a six and considered bumping it near the end. It has a unusual POV and the color palette (especially in the top third of the image is terrific - the yellows are perfect against the green and blue. I suspect what didn''t work so well for voters was the heavily weighted dark bottom portion that is an artifact of the POV. There''s also the contrast of larger dominant shapes at the top and more detailed busy shapes at the bottom. This tends to create ambiguity about where the viewer''s central focus of attention should be. I liked the effect of imbalance in the two halves, it may have been distracting to others.', '2015-06-26 20:43:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7373832, 1151779, 115814, '<td valign="top">Hi Janine, <br/> <br/>Me again, as a Critique Club commenter... The color palette is lovely and the sense of horizontal layering of subject and color change works well together. I think it''s really hard to nail a sunset that doesn''t get a sort of "meh" reaction here, though. We see so many that they tend to lose impact. I know that''s true for me. I become hyper critical of them because they''re so common. Most tend to be highly saturated with exaggerated colors. Perhaps this is in lieu of dramatic subject interest. Your photo has several layers of interest including the dog and walker, yet they are small and lack real impact. It might be improved somewhat by lightening the bottom (dark sand) layer to reveal a bit more detail in the shadows. For me the best thing here is the violet shading at the top and the gradient changes moving down through the golden yellows of the wet sand.</td>', 'Hi Janine,  Me again, as a Critique Club commenter... The color palette is lovely and the sense of horizontal layering of subject and color change works well together. I think it''s really hard to nail a sunset that doesn''t get a sort of "meh" reaction here, though. We see so many that they tend to lose impact. I know that''s true for me. I become hyper critical of them because they''re so common. Most tend to be highly saturated with exaggerated colors. Perhaps this is in lieu of dramatic subject interest. Your photo has several layers of interest including the dog and walker, yet they are small and lack real impact. It might be improved somewhat by lightening the bottom (dark sand) layer to reveal a bit more detail in the shadows. For me the best thing here is the violet shading at the top and the gradient changes moving down through the golden yellows of the wet sand.', '2015-06-26 20:56:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7373923, 1151625, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Breview<br/> <br/>Color Saturation and Hue:  colors are realistic, saturation is not overly done, and hues appear accurate for the subject.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  focus is tack sharp and depth of field is quite deep, which is well suited to the subject.<br/> <br/>Brightness and contrast:  both are well done, but dynamic range seems a tiny bit short.  This results in a burned out area around the sun.  <br/> <br/>There is also a tiny bit of lens flare observable in the middle of the beach near the bend in the stream.  <br/> <br/>Subjective:  this is an excellent image, as noted by the top three finish.  I feel like I can almost feel the granularity of the sand. The use of a slow shutter speed adds to the image.  Though I have to admit I do not associate the sea shore with silence.  Still, excellent work, and congratulations on a well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'Critique Club Breview Color Saturation and Hue:  colors are realistic, saturation is not overly done, and hues appear accurate for the subject. Focus and depth of field:  focus is tack sharp and depth of field is quite deep, which is well suited to the subject. Brightness and contrast:  both are well done, but dynamic range seems a tiny bit short.  This results in a burned out area around the sun.   There is also a tiny bit of lens flare observable in the middle of the beach near the bend in the stream.   Subjective:  this is an excellent image, as noted by the top three finish.  I feel like I can almost feel the granularity of the sand. The use of a slow shutter speed adds to the image.  Though I have to admit I do not associate the sea shore with silence.  Still, excellent work, and congratulations on a well deserved ribbon.', '2015-06-27 01:20:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7373948, 1151297, 115814, '<td valign="top">Hey Mykkka,<br/> <br/>This is a Critique Club comment. I really like the details in the photo. There''s a story here for sure. Friday afternoon, the tie is off, the shoes are off, a cup of coffee (or ???) and a moment of quiet (with the phone on manual silence mode) at the end of the week. It''s a really clever image. But... as you''ve no doubt seen, the majority of voters here are not kind to this type of image and your score shows that. If you look at the highest scoring shots, you''ll see much attention to traditional techniques and "pretty" images.<br/> <br/>So, for my taste, I like the story here and don''t care so much about "pretty." If you''re comfortable with that, this kind of image may find a following of some like minded photographers. If you''re out to get competive scores, that''s a different process and the critique could be quite different. Since you''re new here, I didn''t want to presume. Hope you keep participating and finding your niche. <br/> <br/>- Bill</td>', 'Hey Mykkka, This is a Critique Club comment. I really like the details in the photo. There''s a story here for sure. Friday afternoon, the tie is off, the shoes are off, a cup of coffee (or ???) and a moment of quiet (with the phone on manual silence mode) at the end of the week. It''s a really clever image. But... as you''ve no doubt seen, the majority of voters here are not kind to this type of image and your score shows that. If you look at the highest scoring shots, you''ll see much attention to traditional techniques and "pretty" images. So, for my taste, I like the story here and don''t care so much about "pretty." If you''re comfortable with that, this kind of image may find a following of some like minded photographers. If you''re out to get competive scores, that''s a different process and the critique could be quite different. Since you''re new here, I didn''t want to presume. Hope you keep participating and finding your niche.  - Bill', '2015-06-27 02:07:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7373949, 1151026, 115814, '<td valign="top">Hi Amy Elle,<br/> <br/>Seems you''re an IR fan, although this one is quite different than your graveyard entry in terms of IR toning. I''m personally not an IR fan, but the effect in this shot is effective. Your comments regarding gentleness of the tips is right on and your title hints at this intent. I see you''re pretty new here - you''ll find every kind of style imaginable among the members and registered users, but the styles that are more artistic don''t tend to do as well as more traditional photos - which I''m sure you''ve seen by reviewing the winners and scoring. There are plenty of folks around that appreciate your style of work (if your first two entries are representative of what you like to shoot/process). Hope you find a niche here. It''s a pretty interesting community. Welcome.</td>', 'Hi Amy Elle, Seems you''re an IR fan, although this one is quite different than your graveyard entry in terms of IR toning. I''m personally not an IR fan, but the effect in this shot is effective. Your comments regarding gentleness of the tips is right on and your title hints at this intent. I see you''re pretty new here - you''ll find every kind of style imaginable among the members and registered users, but the styles that are more artistic don''t tend to do as well as more traditional photos - which I''m sure you''ve seen by reviewing the winners and scoring. There are plenty of folks around that appreciate your style of work (if your first two entries are representative of what you like to shoot/process). Hope you find a niche here. It''s a pretty interesting community. Welcome.', '2015-06-27 02:17:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7416267, 1151328, 34659, '<td valign="top">How sweet.  I wonder if they have imprinted on you.  They are so cute!<br/></td>', 'How sweet.  I wonder if they have imprinted on you.  They are so cute!', '2015-11-15 10:40:03.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
